theory.intro:
When you know **two sides and the angle between them** (the included angle), the area is $A=\tfrac{1}{2}ab\sin C$ — no perpendicular height is needed. Rearranged, the same rule finds a missing side when the area is given.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{angles, quotes}
\coordinate (V) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (4.0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (1.4,2.8);
\fill[black!8] (V)--(B)--(A)--cycle;
\draw (V)--(B) node[midway,below] {$a$};
\draw (V)--(A) node[midway,above left] {$b$};
\draw (B)--(A);
\node at (2.1,1.0) {$A$};
\pic[draw,"$C$",angle radius=0.7cm,angle eccentricity=1.7] {angle=B--V--A};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

