A triangular paddock has an area of $70$ m$^{2}$. One side is $12$ m and the included angle is $55^{\circ}$. Find the length $b$ of the other side forming that angle, correct to $2$ decimal places.

development.solution_text:
$A=\dfrac{1}{2}ab\sin C$
$70=\dfrac{1}{2}(12)(b)\sin 55^{\circ}$
$70=6b\sin 55^{\circ}$
$b=\dfrac{70}{6\sin 55^{\circ}}$
$\approx 14.24\text{ m}$
